@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "osb.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki To OSB Account Integration
	Testing to assure that koroneiki account integration to OSB and Project Details works properly.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Kchild - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Oneiki - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the third default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Ochild - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the fourth default user ID variable
	* I tear down the teams on koroneiki with the following names
	| Koroneiki Partner |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Kchild - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Ochild - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Korone - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Oneiki - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| KCHILDKCHILD |
	| OCHILDOCHILD |
	| KORONEKORONE |
	| ONEIKIONEIKI |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Limited Subscription"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| KCHILDKCHILD |
	| OCHILDOCHILD |
	| KORONEKORONE |
	| ONEIKIONEIKI |
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Kchild - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Ochild - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Korone - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Oneiki - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId3}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId4}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: Create T4 account with DXP
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	Testing the ability to create a T4 tiered project on Koroneiki with DXP that later gets synced to OSB

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                         | |
	| Contact Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Language              | English                              | |
	| Name                  | Korone - ${staticProjectName}        | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Profile Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                        | |
	| Status                | Active                               | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the support organization with the code "KORONEKORONE" should be part of the support site
	When I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	Then I should be able to view a project with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and following values
	| Koroneiki Account Key | Obtain from project name      |
	| Project Name          | Korone - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                  |
	| Tier                  | T4                            |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki |
	When I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the keyword "Korone"
	And I go to the project with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	Then the project details with the following values should be visible
	| Project Code    | KORONEKORONE          |
	| State           | ACTIVE                |
	| Level           | Platinum Subscription |
	| Support Region  | United States         |
	| Tier            | T4                    |
	When I go to the History tab
	And I generate the account ID value for "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	Then the history entry with the keyword "Added Account" with the field value "contactEmailAddress" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer        |
	| Update Summary              | Added Account                        |
	| Update Date                 | Today                                |
	| Update Field Name           | contactEmailAddress                  |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Added Account" with the field value "internal" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Added Account                 |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | internal                      |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | false                         |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Added Account" with the field value "code" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Added Account                 |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | code                          |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | KORONEKORONE                  |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Added Account" with the field value "region" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Added Account                 |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | region                        |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | United States                 |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Added Account" with the field value "description" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Added Account                 |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | description                   |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | Test osb account on koroneiki |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Added Account" with the field value "parentAccountId" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Added Account                 |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | parentAccountId               |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | 0                             |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Added Account" with the field value "tier" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Added Account                 |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | tier                          |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | T4                            |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Added Account" with the field value "website" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Added Account                 |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | website                       |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | www.koroneikicorporation.com  |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Added Account" with the field value "accountId" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Added Account                 |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | accountId                     |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | ${staticAccountId}            |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Added Account" with the field value "phoneNumber" should be visible with the following values
